codex
I found a concrete design gap in the accepted adapter boundary: both Apple adapters currently wrap `readPackets` in a non-cancellable continuation and silently truncate mismatched packet/protocol arrays via `zip`. I’m treating that as a separate atomic prerequisite, and I also verified the Darwin errno alias: `EWOULDBLOCK` is literally `EAGAIN`, so observability must use one canonical “would block” counter rather than pretend the kernel can distinguish them.
